    '#### 5.1.2 Backward Engineering (Code to Model)','The tool reflects the compiled domain assembly into engineering/CodeToModel.json. The current immutable properties and state/recovery methods can be compared with the forward model.',
    '#### 5.1.3 Code Map','engineering/DomainCodeMap.dgml contains reflected property dependencies from the actual assembly. Open it in supporting Visual Studio graph tooling. Actual Visual Studio operations and screenshots still require capture in a supporting installed edition; see docs/visual-studio-demo.md.',
    '### 5.2 GitHub & AI Tooling (10 marks)','#### 5.2.1 Source Control',f'Confirmed GitHub account: {PROFILE}. The account URL is not a project repository. No genuine group repository, branch/PR history or contribution figures have been supplied. Local main has no commits. The proposed workflow uses feature branches, student-authored commits, peer review and Pull Requests into main; no historical teamwork is invented.',
    '#### 5.2.2 AI Assistance: Copilot Prompt Documentation',table(['Tool / date','Actual request summary','Kept / changed','Validation'],[['Codex / 23 Oct 2026','Complete PDFs and rubric','Code, tests, workbook and numbered report','Build, MSTest and SQL demo'],['Codex / 23 Oct 2026','Upgrade all UI/UX and functional demos','Three application interfaces and safe workflow states','Native and browser captures'],['image_gen / 23 Oct 2026','Joyful MetroGo 3D transit scene','Original art + 30-second motion graphics','Image inspection; video metadata']]),
    '#### 5.2.3 Reflection on AI Use','AI accelerated scaffolding, but review exposed account lockout, cancellation, stale-stock and template-compliance gaps. These were corrected and tested. Students must understand the submitted code; prompts, assumptions and generated art are declared.',
    '### 5.3 Demo Application (10 marks)',table(['Input / action','Observed or enforced result'],[['Route choice','Active SQL catalogue and immutable fare snapshot'],['Card / Bank QR / Wallet','Labeled simulator terminal or transaction-bound QR'],['Approved','One saved ticket and barcode'],['Declined','No usable ticket; retry possible'],['Timeout','Unknown state; reconcile before a fresh payment'],['Uncertain save','Retry the same reference without duplicate ticket'],['Printer fault','Same-ticket recovery or recorded simulated refund'],['Print','PrintDocument preview; optional OS print']]),
    f'{len(tests(1))} meaningful domain tests passed. Build and SQL-connected screenshots provide local demo evidence. Card/bank/wallet authorization, reconciliation and refund remain simulations. Physical paper output is not tested.',
    image('Actual successful SQL ticket demo','screenshots/tvm-complete-v4.png'),image('Recorded MSTest console output rendered for readability','screenshots/unit-tests-final.png'),
    '## 6. Checklist for "LabGroup_QT2_Assignment1.pdf"',table(['Supplied rubric task','Section','Status'],[[b,d,e] for a,b,c,d,e in A1]),
    'The separate Assignment 1 brief referenced by the template was not among the five supplied files. This checklist audits the supplied report/workbook templates and does not assert review of an unavailable additional brief.',
